# Chrome Extension (Manifest V3) Standards

## Manifest V3 Architecture
- Use background Service Workers (`background.js` / `background.ts`) instead of persistent background scripts.
- Declare minimal permissions in `manifest.json` (e.g., `"activeTab"`, `"storage"`, `"scripting"`).
- Maintain strict Content Security Policy (CSP): do not use `eval()` or load external scripts remotely.

## Chrome APIs & Authentication
- Manage message communication between popup and service workers using `chrome.runtime.sendMessage` and `chrome.runtime.onMessage.addListener`.
- Capture the active browser tab URL and title using `chrome.tabs.query({ active: true, currentWindow: true })`.
- Synchronize and persist Supabase authentication session tokens locally using `chrome.storage.local`.